# FX Exchange — Multi-Currency Trading Platform

A simulated multi-currency trading platform built for the University of Glasgow Internet Technology (M) coursework. The application allows retail users to manage GBP-based currency holdings, execute market trades, place limit orders, and view trade history. Administrators can manage currencies and update exchange rates manually or via CSV import.

---

## Project Structure

```
fx_api/                  - Django REST API (backend)
FXExchange_frontend/     -  React 19 SPA (frontend)
```

---

## Backend — Django REST API

### Tech Stack

| Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Python 3.13 | Language |
| Django 5 | Web framework |
| Django REST Framework | API layer |
| djangorestframework-simplejwt | JWT authentication |
| SQLite | Database |

### Prerequisites

- Python 3.10+
- pip

### Setup & Run

```bash
# 1. Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/sumit-gla-uog/fx_api.git
cd fx_api

# 2. Create and activate virtual environment
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate        # Mac / Linux
.venv\Scripts\activate           # Windows

# 3. Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 4. Apply migrations
python manage.py migrate

# 5. Create a superuser (optional — for Django admin panel)
python manage.py createsuperuser

# 6. Run the development server
python manage.py runserver
```

The API will be available at `http://127.0.0.1:8000`

### Running Tests

```bash
# Run all backend tests (115 tests)
python manage.py test api

# Run specific test file
python manage.py test api.tests.test_models
python manage.py test api.tests.test_views
python manage.py test api.tests.test_admin_models
python manage.py test api.tests.test_admin_views
```

### Key API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| POST | `/api/v1/auth/signup/` | Register a new user |
| POST | `/api/v1/auth/login/` | Login and get JWT tokens |
| POST | `/api/v1/auth/refresh/` | Refresh access token |
| GET | `/api/v1/auth/me/` | Get current user info |
| GET | `/api/v1/currencies/` | List enabled currencies |
| GET | `/api/v1/pairs/` | List currency pairs with rates |
| GET | `/api/v1/portfolio/` | Get user portfolio holdings |
| POST | `/api/v1/portfolio/deposit/` | Simulated GBP deposit |
| POST | `/api/v1/trades/market/` | Execute a market trade |
| GET | `/api/v1/trades/` | List user trades |
| POST | `/api/v1/orders/limit/` | Place a limit order |
| GET | `/api/v1/orders/` | List user orders |
| POST | `/api/v1/orders/<id>/cancel/` | Cancel an open order |
| GET | `/api/v1/admin/dashboard/` | Admin stats overview |
| GET | `/api/v1/admin/currencies/` | List all currencies (admin) |
| POST | `/api/v1/admin/currencies/add/` | Add a new currency (admin) |
| PATCH | `/api/v1/admin/currencies/<id>/toggle/` | Enable/disable currency (admin) |
| POST | `/api/v1/admin/rates/manual/` | Manually update exchange rate (admin) |
| POST | `/api/v1/admin/rates/csv/` | Bulk update rates via CSV (admin) |

### Environment Variables

No `.env` file is required for local development — the backend runs with SQLite out of the box.

For production, set the following:

```env
SECRET_KEY=your-django-secret-key
DEBUG=False
ALLOWED_HOSTS=your-domain.com
```

### Seeding Initial Data (Optional)

To add currencies and pairs manually, use the Admin Rate Management API endpoints after creating an admin user, or use the Django admin panel at `http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin`.

---

## Frontend — React SPA

### Tech Stack

| Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|
| React 19 + TypeScript | UI framework |
| Vite 5 | Build tool |
| Salt DS | UI component library |
| AG Grid | Data tables (portfolio, orders, history, pairs) |
| Highcharts | Rate history chart on pair detail page |
| SWR | API data fetching and caching |
| React Router v6 | Client-side routing |
| React Hook Form | Form management and validation |
| React Dropzone | CSV file drag-and-drop upload |

### Prerequisites

- Node.js 18+
- npm

### Setup & Run

```bash
# 1. Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/sumit-gla-uog/FXExchange_frontend.git
cd FXExchange_frontend

# 2. Install dependencies
npm install

# 3. Create environment file
cp .env.example .env.development     # or create manually (see below)

# 4. Start the development server
npm run dev
```

The app will be available at `http://localhost:5173`

### Environment Variables

Create a `.env.development` file in the project root:

```env
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
```

For production deployment (e.g. Render):

```env
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-backend.onrender.com
```

### Build for Production

```bash
npm run build
# Output will be in the dist/ folder
```

### Running Tests

```bash
# Run all frontend tests
npm run test

# Run tests with coverage report
npm run coverage
```

### Project Structure

```
src/
├── api/            ← API client, auth helpers, SWR fetcher
├── auth/           ← RequireAuth route guard
├── components/
│   ├── grids/      ← AG Grid cell renderers
│   └── ui/         ← Reusable components (CurrencyCard, StatCard, etc.)
├── hooks/
│   ├── customer/   ← useDashboard, usePairs, useDeposit, etc.
│   └── useSignup   ← Signup hook
├── pages/
│   ├── admin/      ← Admin dashboard, currencies, rates pages
│   ├── customer/   ← Dashboard, portfolio, pairs, orders, history pages
│   ├── Loginpage/  ← Login page
│   ├── SignupPage/ ← Sign up page
│   └── SelectRolePage/ ← Role selection after login
├── styles/         ← Global CSS and AG Grid overrides
├── test/           ← Vitest + React Testing Library tests
└── types/          ← TypeScript type definitions
```

---

## Running Both Together (Local Development)

Open two terminal windows:

**Terminal 1 — Backend:**
```bash
cd fx_api
source .venv/bin/activate
python manage.py runserver
```

**Terminal 2 — Frontend:**
```bash
cd FXExchange_frontend
npm run dev
```

Then open `http://localhost:5173` in your browser.

### First Time Setup

1. Go to `http://localhost:5173/signup` and create a **Customer** account
2. To create an **Admin** account, either:
   - Sign up and then use the Django shell to set `is_staff=True`
   - Or use `python manage.py createsuperuser`
3. Log in and select your role
4. As a **Customer**: deposit simulated GBP, then browse pairs and trade
5. As an **Admin**: add currencies and update exchange rates before customers can trade

